11. DRY Principle
DRY = Don't Repeat Yourself

Definition

Every piece of knowledge or logic should exist in only one place in your code.

Bad Example
let total1 = 10 + 20;
let total2 = 10 + 20;
let total3 = 10 + 20;
The same logic is repeated.

Good Example
function add(a, b) {
    return a + b;
}

console.log(add(10, 20));
console.log(add(10, 20));
console.log(add(10, 20));
The logic is written once and reused.

